.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=FarYaml

@Contents
$^#FarYaml: YAML Browser#

 FarYaml is a LuaMacro panel module for browsing YAML files.

   ~Installation~@Install@

   ~Description~@Description@

   ~Panel: columns, names, sorting~@Panel@

   ~Comments~@Comments@

   ~Keyboard commands~@Keyboard@

   ~Editing (F4)~@Edit@

   ~Copy (F5)~@Copy@

   ~Command line~@CmdLine@

   ~Errors in YAML files~@Errors@

   ~Limitations~@Limits@

@Install
$^#Installation#

 1. From the #lua# directory, build the bundle:

   #make bundle LUAJIT=C:/Apps/Far3/luajit.exe#

 2. Copy #faryaml.lua# together with both HLF files
 to a directory of your choice under #%FARPROFILE%\Macros\scripts\#.
 Keep all three files together. The bundle includes all Lua modules.

 Reload LuaMacro macros or restart FAR.

@Description
$^#Description#

 This LuaMacro module shows the contents of a YAML file as an archive. Mappings
 and sequences are shown as "folders", scalar values as "files".

 Press #Enter# on a file with the .yaml or .yml extension to open it. To
 leave the document press #Enter# on ".." in its root. The file itself is
 changed only by ~F4~@Edit@; all other operations are read-only.

 A file with several documents (separated by ---) is shown as a
 sequence of documents named [0], [1], ...

 You can also open a file from the ~command line~@CmdLine@.

@Panel
$^#Panel: columns, names, sorting#

 #Columns#

   #Key#          name of the key; list items are named [0], [1], ...
   #Type#         map, seq, str, int, float, bool or null
   #Value#        the value of a scalar; {N} for a mapping with N keys,
                 [N] for a sequence with N items; line breaks are shown
                 as the pilcrow character, long values are cut
   #Description#  the ~comment~@Comments@ of the entry

 #Names#

 Names are made valid for file names, so F3, F5 and Quick View work:
 the characters / \ : are replaced by look-alike Unicode characters,
 the characters * ? " < > | by _. Equal names get the suffix (2), (3)
 and so on.

 #Order and sorting#

 The panel opens unsorted, i.e. in the order of the file. Sorting by
 extension (#Ctrl-F4#) sorts by the #Type# column, sorting by description
 (#Ctrl-F10#) sorts by the #Description# column. Other sort modes work
 as usual.

 The panel title shows the file name and the path inside the document.

@Comments
$^#Comments#

 The comments of the YAML file are shown in the #Description# column:

   - the comment at the end of the line with the key or the list item
   - the comment lines right above the entry (no blank line between them)

 @-
  ## Example
  pylint:
      jobs: 1  ## one process
 @+

 Here "Example" is the description of #pylint#, "one process" - of #jobs#.

 The sign ## inside quotes and inside block scalars (| and >) is text,
 not a comment. F3 and F5 use the original source fragment when its range
 can be determined; generated YAML may not retain comments or formatting.
 For entries given through aliases the description can be inexact.

@Keyboard
$^#Keyboard commands#

 #Enter#     On a .yaml/.yml file: open it. On a section: enter it.

 #F3#        On a section or on "..": view its YAML text (with comments) in
             the viewer. "..": the whole current section.
             On a value: view the value.

 #F4#        On a key, section, list item or "..": ~edit~@Edit@ it; the
             changes are written to the file.

 #F5#        ~Copy~@Copy@ the selected items to a YAML file.

 #Ctrl-F4#   Sort by Type (the Extension sort mode).
 #Ctrl-F10#  Sort by Description.

 #F1#        Show a brief command summary.

@Edit
$^#Editing (F4)#

 F4 opens the YAML text of the entry in the FAR editor: the key with
 its value, comments included. After you save and close the editor the
 text replaces the entry in the file. The rest of the file stays as it
 was byte for byte; the encoding (UTF-8, BOM, UTF-16) and line breaks
 are kept. The panel is updated and you stay in the same section.

 You can rename the key, add neighbour keys or delete the entry (leave
 the text empty). F4 on ".." edits the whole current section (in the
 root - the whole file).

 The file is not changed and the dialog "changes were not saved" with
 the buttons #Edit again# and #Discard# is shown when:

   - the result is not valid YAML (the line is shown);
   - the file is read-only;
   - the file was changed on disk after the panel was opened;
   - you delete the first key of a list item (the dash would be lost).

 F4 is disabled for aliases, merge-derived entries, complex mapping
 keys, and nodes inside flow collections {...} [...]. The panel shows a
 message; use F4 on their parent section to edit the source text.

@Copy
$^#Copy (F5)#

 F5 shows the copy dialog and writes the selected items to a YAML file.
 The file name is proposed as #key.yaml#; you may enter another file name
 or a folder. If the file exists you are asked about overwriting. The
 YAML file being browsed cannot be overwritten.

 Several selected keys of a mapping are written to one file
 (#section-selection.yaml#), several list items - as a list. Comments are
 kept. Move and delete do not change the YAML file.

@CmdLine
$^#Command line#

 The prefix #yaml:# opens any file, not only .yaml/.yml:

 @-
  #yaml:C:\configs\config.yaml#
  #yaml:"C:\my configs\a.yml"#
 @+

@Errors
$^#Errors in YAML files#

 If you press Enter on a file with invalid YAML, a dialog shows the
 file name, the line and the message of the parser. The
 button #Edit# opens the file in the FAR editor at the line of the error.

 Such a file does not open in the FarYaml panel. Use F3 or F4 in the
 regular FAR file panel to view or edit its source. Search and Quick View
 do not show the errors.

@Limits
$^#Limitations#

   - File size is limited to 64 MiB.
   - Parsing uses the pure Lua Xmake YAML addon parser (v1.0.0); YAML 1.2 is not fully implemented.
   - UTF-32 files are read-only in FarYaml, but comments remain visible.
   - F4 does not save flow collections {...} [...], aliases, merged entries, or complex mapping keys.
   - Complex YAML constructs should be checked against the parser limitations.
